    "body": "<!-- linear-linkback -->\n<details>\n<summary><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4531/sub2api-a-missing-component-price-zeroes-the-whole-requests-billing\">TXE-4531 sub2api: a missing component price zeroes the whole request's billing (DeepSeek cache reads billed at 0)</a></summary>\n<p>\n\n## What happened\n\nOn 2026-10-16 16:17–17:14 (+08) production logged 32 `openai_chat_completions.record_usage_failed` errors: `calculate materialized pricing for model deepseek-v4-pro: pricing unavailable for model \"deepseek-v4-pro\": missing cache read price` (user 133, key 143, group 23, accounts 2709 and 2711). usage_logs has 33 deepseek-v4-pro rows billed at 0 in that window, every one with cache_read_tokens > 0.\n\nThe same gap hit `deepseek-v4.1-flash` earlier: 1647 rows billed at 0 between 2026-10-09 and 2026-10-14, all with cache reads.\n\n## Cause\n\n* Data: channel 6 (DeepSeek) pricing rows 147, 148, 149, 150 (deepseek-v4-flash-0731, deepseek-v4-pro-0813, deepseek-v4.1-flash, deepseek-v4-pro) have input and output prices and no cache read price.\n* Code: `validateTokenPricing` (`billing_service.go`) rejects the whole request when any used component price is missing, so input and output are not billed either.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- ☐ R1 A missing component price bills that component at 0; every priced component is billed. A warning log names the model and the unpriced components.\n- ☐ R2 A model with no pricing row still fails as today.\n- ☐ R3 Tests: cache reads without a cache read price bill input and output; the record-usage path writes a successful, non-zero billing record.\n- ☐ R4 Production prices: cache read prices for rows 147–150 from the official DeepSeek price table (written by the user).\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRe-billing the historical zero-cost rows.\n</p>\n</details>\n<!-- linear-review-link -->\n<p><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/review/fixbilling-txe-4531-a-missing-component-price-bills-that-component-at-4ff9194b7191\">Review in Linear</a></p>\n",
